WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.814 --> 00:00:09.462
This page is your course map. Every week is a station on one journey, and everything else on the site hangs off this page.

2
00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:18.079
Find the current week. The highlighted station is where the course is right now. Click any station to open that week's page.

3
00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:29.089
Read the station badge before you click. Each station shows how that week runs, for example how many readings it carries or that it is a focus week with no new material.

4
00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:39.907
Use the Study Compass. The compass box suggests what to do next based on what you have already visited on this device. It is a suggestion, never a requirement.

5
00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:50.923
Search when you know what you want. The search box finds readings, concepts, and scholars across the whole course, so you do not have to remember which week something lives in.

6
00:00:50.923 --> 00:01:01.926
Pick your program lens if you want one. The Viewing as chip personalizes examples to your field of study. The course content stays the same for everyone; only the framing changes. You can turn it off any time.

7
00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:06.612
Nothing on this page is graded or reported to your professor.

8
00:01:06.612 --> 00:01:12.971
Where next: Open the current week's station and start with its Before you begin section.
